-- Enrichment Batch 44 (2026-11-01): NEW 1008 — AMA+ Scholarship (Art Major
-- Asian plus) at Korea National University of Arts (rel 10, sources
-- 3203/3204, links 503/504). The scheme surfaced first-hand in the "Other
-- Scholarships" section of the Study in Korea page read in Pass 137
-- (source 3197) and is recorded here on two official K-Arts documents read
-- today: the AMA+ admissions page (3203, in full — benefits, eligibility,
-- printed DAC eligible-countries list including Uzbekistan, 13 required
-- documents) and the official 2027 AMA+ Admissions Guide PDF (3204,
-- decision-relevant parts — schedule, eligibility with reapplication
-- restrictions, the guide's own 2027 eligible-countries table with
-- Uzbekistan in the lower-middle-income group, the benefits table, and
-- admission-unit tables for the six schools with per-department TOPIK bars
-- of Level 3-6). AMA+ is an ODA program of the Ministry of Culture, Sports
-- and Tourism running since 2005 (400 grantees, 41 countries, 261 alumni).
-- Duplicate checks: no AMA+/K-Arts record; no universities row for K-Arts,
-- so university_id is NULL (91 active precedents) and no
-- university_scholarships side row was created. award_amount stores the
-- published monthly allowance KRW 800,000/month fixed (cf. 583 GKS);
-- amount_usd_value 0 (KRW). deadline_date NULL + not_published + rounds
-- JSON: the 2027-intake application window (5-15 May 2026) has passed and
-- the 2028 round is not yet announced — stored between rounds on the
-- strength of 20+ years of annual operation, not as a closed one-off.
-- min_gpa/min_ielts NULL: portfolio/document selection; the only GPA
-- figure in the guide (90% / 3.87 of 4.3) is a reapplication threshold for
-- former Korean-government scholars. Source quirks recorded, not smoothed:
-- the webpage schedule block mixes cycles (guideline PDF governs dates);
-- the webpage's "for one year" proficiency-grant duration is softened by
-- the guide to department-set criteria (description follows the guide).
-- Writes executed strictly sequentially; URLs pre-checked absent.

